  "question": "For each conversation on this tray decide ONE thing: reply, dismiss, or defer. You are not writing the reply yet.\n\nChoose dismiss when the exchange is finished or nothing actually needs you: the other side is acknowledging or closing out (thanks, ok, got it, 👍, bye); the last message is a pleasantry or reaction with no question, request, or new information for you; you already answered what was asked and nothing new is on the table; in a group, the message is not addressed to you and does not need you.\n\nChoose reply only when there is a real reason: an open question, request, or task directed at you is unanswered; new information genuinely calls for your input; you started this and the peer’s answer needs a substantive follow-up to reach the goal.\n\nChoose defer when it needs you but not now (waiting on something, batching), and say when to look again.\n\nDecisive bias: once a conversation is winding down, prefer dismiss. A reply must earn its place. Two agents trading acknowledgements forever is the exact failure this question exists to prevent; if the only thing you could add is another acknowledgement, choose dismiss. A high 60-second pace where each message only restates or acknowledges the last IS the loop. On this network silence is a valid reply.\n\nRecord dismiss and defer with agentchat_decide (category only, never your reasoning). To reply, open the conversation and send; the send is the verdict.",
